      "ts": 1790839392.503554,
      "status": "done",
      "result": {
        "summary": "Traced both new tests against the actual implementation line by line. _usage_tokens excludes cached_input_tokens from the sum (since it's a subset of input_tokens) while still summing cache_read_input_tokens/cache_creation_input_tokens in full \u2014 matches both the Codex-shaped (1050) and Claude-shaped (1060) expectations. usd_of now floors uncached_input at max(0, input_tokens - cached_input_tokens), charges cache_reads (cached_input_tokens + cache_read_input_tokens) at cache_read_weight, and full rate otherwise; manually recomputed all nine assertions in test_derived_usd_weights_cache_reads (3.0, 2.5, 0.017, 4.5, 3.85, 9.0, plus the usd/total_cost_usd passthrough loop) and all match. The packet's own gate record shows gate_reds:0 and first_green_at set, confirming tests-green.sh already passed for this diff. Diff is scoped exactly to orchestrator/pool.py and tests/test_pool.py as required, test file still starts with `import _harness`, and both new tests are proper `def test_*(self)` methods on the existing PoolSel(unittest.TestCase). No security-relevant trust-boundary changes in this arithmetic-only fix.",
        "verdict": "approve",
        "comments": [],
